  "visualReview": {
    "status": "Candidate only; not accepted",
    "neutral": "2px hard mask removes almost all neutral Iris clipping (Left 0, Right 4 opaque pixels still omitted). Existing Eye/Iris RGBA are unchanged.",
    "gaze": "No large spill outside the eye opening was seen at the supplied poses. Small lower-edge pale fragments/double lines remain; these are not fully explained by mask omission. At +7.8/-3 the viewer-left iris still meets an abrupt right-side cut.",
    "eyeliner": "No broad overpainting of the upper lashes was visible at review scale. Dilation expands the clipping region near the lash seam, and the separate conservative overlap counts must be checked in Cubism with actual draw order; absence of overlap is not certified.",
    "suggestion": "Use the 2px candidate only for controlled visual comparison with the current model. Do not treat this texture diagnostic as model acceptance."
  },
  "outputScope": "PNG alpha masks and diagnostic previews only; no PSD, GUI or import."
